════════ G6 ADVERSARIAL PROBE — belt 2 across sessions (beyond done_when) ════════
Scenario: device-a redeemed a code in an EARLIER session (server: codes.redeemed_by=device-a,
accepted attempt row landed). Local store then lost (iOS PWA storage eviction — fresh RxDB db
by construction). Crew re-scans the SAME code on device-a today.
Driver/probe: scratchpad c3-g6/belt2-drive.sh + belt2-probe.mjs (production modules:
push-replication.js handler + replicas.js codes pull replica; spike-supabase substrate,
RECONCILE; probe rows cleaned up after).

Transcript (verbatim):
  == last week: device-a redeems the code ==
  [{"ok":true,"reason":null}]
  == last week: attempt row landed accepted (HTTP code below) ==
  201
  == today: fresh session, store evicted, re-scan of the used code ==
  # codes replica pulled: redeemed_by=device-a redeemed_at=2026-09-04T23:03:56.465996+00:00
  # enqueue: deduped=false (fresh store — dedupe cannot see last week's attempt)
  # NEW attempt after push: status=accepted reason=- winner_device=- landed=true
  PROBE RESULT: BUG — the re-scan of an ALREADY-USED code was arbitrated ACCEPTED (belt 2
  unbounded); UI shows "redeemed ok" instead of F3's "already used"
  == server attempt rows for the one code ==
  device-a|accepted|-
  device-a|accepted|-
  ACCEPTED_ROWS_FOR_ONE_CODE=2
  (probe rows cleaned up)

Finding: belt 2 (own-device already_used = accepted) has NO time bound — it cannot distinguish
"this attempt's lost burn" from "we redeemed this code in ANY past session". The enqueue dedupe
that merge-intent engineering call #4 leans on only holds while the local store survives; the
slate's own binding build-fact prescribed the belt shape, so this is a design gap for triage,
not an implementer deviation. Consequence: false "redeemed ✓" at the window (double-serve) +
a second accepted scan_attempts row for one code (§9 audit corruption). Candidate fix: arbitrate
accepted only when the replica's redeemed_at >= this attempt's scanned_at (clock-skew slack);
otherwise rejected/already_used with winner_device = own device ("already used — by you").
